      "content": "It is completely understandable that the fear of losing control makes the idea of \"existing on your own terms\" feel like a dangerous gamble. You are right that the world is built on the expectations of others, and stepping out of that game feels like the only way to stop the pain. But remember that you are not just waiting for a life that never happens; you are the person who has to build it, even if it starts small and feels uncertain. You can try to be yourself without changing everything at once, or you can try to find a way to be yourself that doesn't require you to break the cage. The exit isn't a single button you press; it's a path you can walk one step at a time, and you don't have to finish the whole journey before you feel safe.",
